# Code Owners
#
# Owners listed here are automatically requested for review on matching files,
# which is what makes the "require approvals" rule in docs/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md
# actionable rather than a burden on contributors to remember.
#
# Syntax: <path pattern>  <@user or @org/team>
# Later matching rules win, so put the most specific patterns last.
#
# REPLACE the placeholder below with real owners before relying on this file.
# WARNING: GitHub silently ignores rules naming a user or team without write access,
# so leaving @OWNER-PLACEHOLDER in place produces no error and no reviewer request.
# Verify under Settings > Code owners after editing. See docs/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md.

# Default owner for everything in the repository
* @OWNER-PLACEHOLDER

# Governance documents usually warrant a stricter owner than application code
# /prime_directive.md            @OWNER-PLACEHOLDER
# /PR_REVIEW_CLOSURE_POLICY.md   @OWNER-PLACEHOLDER
# /docs/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md     @OWNER-PLACEHOLDER
# /.github/                      @OWNER-PLACEHOLDER

# Examples for application code — uncomment and adapt
# /src/api/       @your-org/backend-team
# /src/web/       @your-org/frontend-team
# /migrations/    @your-org/data-team
